# Prisma Schema Conventions (Shopping List Backend)

- Uses a PostgreSQL datasource. Connection string is set by the `DATABASE_URL` environment variable.
- Schema includes three main models: `List`, `ListMember`, and `Item`, and an enum `Role`.
- Model conventions:
  - `id` is always a `String` (UUID), set via `@id @default(uuid()) @db.Uuid`.
  - `createdAt`/`updatedAt` fields are present for audit, with relevant Prisma defaults.
  - All `listId`, `userId` references use `@db.Uuid`.
- Relationships:
  - `List` has many `items` and `members`.
  - `Item` and `ListMember` have a required `listId` and link to `List` via a relation with `onDelete: Cascade`.
  - `ListMember` de-duplicates `(listId, userId)` and stores their role (`OWNER` or `EDITOR`).
- Optional fields (e.g., `description`, `quantity`, `unit`, `notes`, `category`, `position`) are suffixed with `?`.
- Enum `Role` is strictly `OWNER` or `EDITOR`.
